            <ArticleTitle>Draft Genome Sequences of Three Aeromonas hydrophila Isolates from Catfish and Tilapia.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">e01509-16</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1128/genomeA.01509-16</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Aeromonas hydrophila is a Gram-negative bacterium that is particularly adapted to freshwater environments and can cause severe infections in fish and humans. Here, we report the draft genomes of three A. hydrophila catfish and tilapia isolates.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright © 2017 Tekedar et al.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
